<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Josiah Harlan</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/josiah">Josiah</a> Harlan was an American adventurer who travelled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punjab">Punjab</a> in the early nineteenth century. He was among the foreign officers employed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ranjit-singh">Ranjit Singh</a>. He is mentioned alongside <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jean-francois-allard">Allard</a>, Court and Ventura as one of the Europeans and Americans who helped train the army of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikh-empire">Sikh Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/josiah-harlan.jpg" alt="Josiah Harlan" width="216" height="321" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:JosiahHarlan.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
